{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/95120-puns-and-preparation","id":95120,"title":"Puns and Preparation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-20T12:12:23-07:00","id":95120,"title":"Puns and Preparation","content":"Play on Words is my favorite power ever. But it's the sort of thing that, unless you're sort of person who's punning constantly, is often going to be a little difficult to use in practice. So this thread is for ideas about how to take advantage of Play on Words through clever preparation. Some of them involve setting situations up where you're likely to get the desired response, some of them involve talking with your fellow PCs beforehand so they're likely to use phrases you need if a particular situation arises. Feel free to respond with more ideas for how to exploit this Exploit.<br /> <br /> 1. Create a gadget mobile phone with an extraplanar pocket and give it to your fellow player. Obtain the contact information for your target and have your friend input it into the phone. Ask your friend if the party has a way to get in touch with your target, and for your fellow player to say, &quot;I've got him in my cell phone.&quot; Imprison the target in your extraplanar cell. Use this trick to summon your friends by flipping open the phone to release them, or to trap enemies in a hard-to-escape prison.<br /> <br /> 2. Wire a bomb to a digital clock, and set the bomb to go off yesterday. Then drive off, and listen to an oldies radio station. As soon as you hear the phrase &quot;Blast from the past,&quot; BOOM!<br /> <br /> 3. Buy a wireless router and install the necessary software on a laptop or mobile phone. If you ever need to remotely hijack a car or a plane or a tank or an aircraft carrier, just open it up and have a friend click Install New Wireless Driver.<br /> <br /> 4. Gain access to expensive or exclusive events for free, just by breaking the speed limit. &quot;I'm sorry, sir, but I'm going to have to give you a ticket.&quot;<br /> <br /> 5. Destroy your enemies by striking up conversations about how attractive they are. If your conversational partner indicates that they are hot, your target bursts into flame or suffers from an inexplicable and fatal fever-use the Damage or Incapacitate options-if you choose a fever option, this is a good way to get someone hospitalized and out of the way, even if you don't manage to kill them. If you're lucky enough to get a more descriptive conversational partner, you may be able to transform your target into a real fox, a stallion, a muffin that tastes like a stallion, a large chunk of some innocuous substance, or even a cougar. For these latter options it'll only last a few hours, but that's definitely enough time to do something useful while your opponent is incapacitated for several hours. Because common parlance has relatively limited and common ways to describe attractive people, this one's pretty reliable.<br /> <br /> 6. Arrange for one of your social-focused allies to regularly tell enraged NPCs who look like they're about to start a fight to &quot;Chill,&quot; so that you can drop their body temperatures to below freezing resulting in incapacitation or damage.<br /> <br /> 7. Talk to your fellow PCs beforehand, so that if someone is ever holding a gun (or a bazooka, or a Magic Staff of Death, or whatever) to your head, you can count on someone telling them that they're holding all the cards. Cards are much less dangerous. Fun way to disarm opponents in a pinch.<br /> <br /> 8. If ever you're up against a group of enemies, which includes a single member who is a member of a racial group, gender, or supernatural splat different than the others, arrange for your allies to point it out. As soon as the target is accused of being the &quot;token Vampire&quot; (or minority, or whatever), turn your opponent into an arcade token with their face on it. One opponent down.<br /> <br /> 9. This one's been pointed out, but in a pinch you can use Marco Polo to get an opponent to say what you need them to say.<br /> <br /> 10. Turn vampires into burning automobiles at every opportunity.<br /> <br /> 11. Enough people will respond to &quot;how are you doing?&quot; with &quot;I'm doing good&quot; that you an pretty reliably expect anonymous donations from their accounts to the charity of your choice.<br /> <br /> 12. Make a gadget shot glass with Merciless Gunman. Wait for the right moment.<br /> <br /> Anyone else have any ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T13:43:23-07:00","id":95184,"title":"","content":"If you can find a practical application for this,I'll be astounded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.nuklearpower.com/2004/01/22/episode-375-thinking-outside-the-box/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.nuklearpower.com/comics/8-bit-theater/040122.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.nuklearpower.com/2004/01/22/episode-375-thinking-outside-the-box/\" target=\"_blank\"> Nuklear Power &raquo; Archive &raquo; Episode 375: Thinking Outside the Box </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.nuklearpower.com/2004/01/22/episode-375-thinking-outside-the-box/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.nuklearpower.com/2004/01/22/episode-375-thinking-outside-the-box/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}